-- title:
--   An Igusa-type valuation ring avoiding a prescribed blow-up end
-- statement:
--   Global data. Fix a prime $q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota \colon L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be (`hH₁`) the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$), with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ equal (`hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Base ring. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ for which $L$ is its fraction field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function (`hj`), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   The finite chart and its supersingular point. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the corresponding algebra for $j^{-1}$ along their common middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with `ιFin` the canonical morphism $\operatorname{Spec} C =$ `XFin` $\to X$. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) and supersingular (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $x \in \Omega$ for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $x$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`. For every point $z$ of $X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the function pulled back from $\varpi$ along `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` $y' = z$ and with $y'$ supersingular in the sense of `hss`, the hypothesis provides: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma \colon A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the second series being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f u\big)$, subject to seven conjuncts. Writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the induced homomorphism $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ through the affine open image of `ιFin`, these are: (a) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (b) every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, i.e. satisfies [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the condition that on every quotient of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, the image of $\tau$ under $\iota$ agrees with the slash action by the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` — preserves $C$; (c) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, then the induced map of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (d) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are $\theta \in \operatorname{Aut}(S)$, $c \in W$ and $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the action of $\tau$ on $C$, $\theta$ fixes the constants $C(w)$, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (e) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $\mathrm{toC}$ followed by $e$ are distinct; (f) for a prime $P$ of $S$ satisfying the same conditions with $(a,b) = (1,0)$ and $a \in C$, the image $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (g) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-series with exponents scaled by $q$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0 \in A$ with the difference lying in $y'$ there are $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that the degree-$e_0$ binary form of $h$ takes unit values at all $(a,b) \in W^2$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\,\cdot\, - a_0)))$ is the class of $h$.
--
--   The chosen point and its chart presentation. Fix such data $z$, $\varpi_z$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), $y'$ (`hy'`, `hss'`) with $y'$ the point $y$ (`hy'y`), and fix a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$ with $\sigma_1 \colon A \to W_1$, $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\big)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for these data exactly the seven conjuncts (a)–(g) listed above.
--
--   The centre, the blow-up chart and the valuation ring $W$. Let $J$ be the ideal of $C$ equal (`hJ`) to the infimum of all ideals of the form: the contraction along the action of $\tau$ on $C$ of the contraction along $\mathrm{toC}$ followed by $\mathrm{germY}$ and $e_1$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ equal (`hB`) to the $C$-algebra generated by $\{\,i/\varpi_t : i \in J\,\}$, and let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypotheses on $B$ and $W$ are: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$; `hR2`, that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W$ meets $L$ exactly in the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if the image of $b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   The Drinfeld-model hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses). First, for every structure of a `GaloisField q 2`-algebra on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho \colon B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by $(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$, whose vanishing locus is the preimage of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ stabilising $W$, there is $c \in (\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2)^{\times}$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $\det \cdot (\,)^{q+1}$) such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c) \circ \rho$ on $B$, and $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity. Second, $B$ is stable under every such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ is reached by some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, in the sense that $\tau$ carries every $b \in B$ whose image lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ into $B$ and into $Q$. Fourth, an element $b \in B$ all of whose images $\tau(b)$ (over $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\tau(b) \in B$) lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by the image of $\varpi$. Fifth, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserves $y$ on $C$, the subring $W$ is stable under $\tau$.
--
--   The end $O$. Let $O$ be a subring of $K$ for which (`hO`) there is $a \in J$, nonzero in $K$, such that, with $B_a$ the $C$-algebra generated by $\{\,i/a : i \in J\,\}$ viewed over $A$, some maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ satisfies: $O$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$; every $b \in y$ has non-invertible image in $O$; and $B$ is not contained in $O$. Assume further $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ local (`hOloc`), $O$ Noetherian (`hOnoe`) and $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`).
--
--   The stability hypothesis `hIgStab`. Every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ which meets $L$ exactly in the image of $A$, for which the image of $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, which contains $C$, and for which some $c \in C$ has the property that for every monic $p \in A[X]$ the value at $c$ of $p$ mapped to $K$ lies in $V$ and outside $\mathfrak{m}_V$, is stable under every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$: $f \in V$ if and only if $\tau f \in V$.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses there exists a valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that: (1) for $x \in L$, the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $V$ if and only if $x$ comes from $A$; (2) the image of $\varpi$ in $K$, whenever it lies in $V$, lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$; (3) $j$ lies in $V$, and for every monic $p \in A[X]$ the value at $j$ of $p$ mapped to $K$, whenever it lies in $V$, lies outside $\mathfrak{m}_V$; (4) there is an element of $O$ not lying in $V$; (5) $C \subseteq V$; and (6) every $b \in C$ whose image lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ lies in $y$.
--
--   This is the existence, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame (a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \bmod 12$ dividing $M'$, with no lower bound imposed on $q$), of an Igusa-type branch through the supersingular point $y$ of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A$: a valuation ring of $K$ restricting to $A$ on $L$, with $\varpi$ in its maximal ideal, with $j$ reducing to an element transcendental over the residue field, containing the chart algebra $C$ with $\mathfrak{m}_V \cap C \subseteq y$, and failing to contain the prescribed end $O$ of the blow-up of $C$ along the weighted centre $J$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_pow_mem_centre_pow_of_labelUnit_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_pow_mem_centre_pow_of_labelUnit_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd), and is deduced from the two companion statements on supersingular primes and the Igusa trichotomy for this frame together with the transcendence criterion [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.forall_monic_aeval_not_mem_maximalIdeal_of_not_isMaximal_centre`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.forall_monic_aeval_not_mem_maximalIdeal_of_not_isMaximal_centre).
